{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-330498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-2,4)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨0,3,-5⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-330498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨1,-2,4⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨0,3,-5⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,3,-5⟩ & =⟨1,-2,4⟩\\cdot ⟨0,3,-5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,3,-5⟩ & =-26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨0,3,-5⟩ & =-26 \\\\ 3y-5z & =-26 \\\\ 3y-5z+26 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-330498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b"} {"question" "q-330498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-330498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3x+y-5z+26=0"] ["math" "3y+5z+26=0"] ["math" "3y-5z+24=0"] ["math" "3y-5z+26=0"] ["math" "3y-5z-26=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-330498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3y-5z+26=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(5,2,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=3i-j+2k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨5,2,-1⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨3,-1,2⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ & =⟨5,2,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ & =11 \\\\ 3x-y+2z & =11 \\\\ 3x-y+2z-11 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b"} {"question" "q-127964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x-3y+z-17=0"] ["math" "2x-y+3z-15=0"] ["math" "3x-2y+z-13=0"] ["math" "3x-y+2z-11=0"] ["math" "x-3y+2z-7=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x-y+2z-11=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-2,1,-3)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨-2,7,-1⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-2,1,-3⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨-2,7,-1⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,7,-1⟩ & =⟨-2,1,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,7,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,7,-1⟩ & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,7,-1⟩ & =14 \\\\ -2x+7y-z & =14 \\\\ -2x+7y-z-14 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b"} {"question" "q-127971" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127971" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2x+7y+z-11=0"] ["math" "-2x+7y-z-14=0"] ["math" "-x+2y-7z-7=0"] ["math" "-x+7y-2z+15=0"] ["math" "7x-2y-z+19=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127971" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2x+7y-z-14=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-2,3,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=3i+4j-k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-2,3,-1⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨3,4,-1⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,4,-1⟩ & =⟨-2,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨3,4,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,4,-1⟩ & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,4,-1⟩ & =7 \\\\ 3x+4y-z & =7 \\\\ 3x+4y-z-7 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b"} {"question" "q-127967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3x+4y-z-7=0"] ["math" "3x-4y-z+9=0"] ["math" "4x+3y-z-11=0"] ["math" "4x-3y-z+13=0"] ["math" "x+3y-4z-17=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-127967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x+4y-z-7=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-33164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-4,3,0)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=2i+5j-8k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-33164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-4,3,0⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨2,5,-8⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,5,-8⟩ & =⟨-4,3,0⟩\\cdot ⟨2,5,-8⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,5,-8⟩ & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,5,-8⟩ & =7 \\\\ 2x+5y-8z & =7 \\\\ 2x+5y-8z-7 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-33164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b"} {"question" "q-33164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-33164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4x+3y+z+7=0"] ["math" "-4x+3y-7=0"] ["math" "2x+5y-8z-17=0"] ["math" "2x+5y-8z-1=0"] ["math" "2x+5y-8z-7=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-33164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x+5y-8z-7=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,-4,1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=-2+t \\\\ y=1+4t \\\\ z=5\\end{aligned}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,-4,1⟩.$  From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨1,4,0⟩.$  So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨1,4,0⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,4,0⟩ & =⟨2,-4,1⟩\\cdot ⟨1,4,0⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,4,0⟩ & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,4,0⟩ & =-14 \\\\ x+4y & =-14 \\\\ x+4y+14 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b"} {"question" "q-336540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x+5y+14=0"] ["math" "x+4y+14=0"] ["math" "x+4y+z+10=0"] ["math" "x+4y-2z+13=0"] ["math" "x-4y+z+14=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x+4y+14=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,-1,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$x\\,-\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$y\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$z\\,-\\,$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,-1,3⟩.$ From the vectorial equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨1,-4,2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨1,-4,2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩ & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩ & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩ & =12 \\\\ x-4y+2z & =12 \\\\ x-4y+2z-12 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b"} {"question" "q-336112" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336112" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336112" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336112" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336112" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336112" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-70809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,3,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-70809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,3,-1⟩.$ From the vectorial equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨3,2,-2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨3,2,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-2⟩ & =⟨2,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-2⟩ & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-2⟩ & =14 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z & =14 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z-14 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-70809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b"} {"question" "q-70809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-70809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2x+y+z-2=0"] ["math" "2x+3y-z-14=0"] ["math" "2x-z-14=0"] ["math" "3x+2y-2z-14=0"] ["math" "3x+2y-2z-2=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-70809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x+2y-2z-14=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336538" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(3,-2,1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n\\frac{x-1}{5}=\\frac{z+2}{-3},\\,y=4\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336538" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,-2,1⟩.$ From the Cartesian equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨5,0,-3⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨5,0,-3⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,0,-3⟩ & =⟨3,-2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨5,0,-3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,0,-3⟩ & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨5,0,-3⟩ & =12 \\\\ 5x-3z & =12 \\\\ 5x-3z-12 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336538" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b"} {"question" "q-336538" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336538" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5x-3z+12=0"] ["math" "5x-3z-12=0"] ["math" "5y-3x+12=0"] ["math" "5y-3z-12=0"] ["math" "x-3z-12=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-336538" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5x-3z-12=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-128375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(3,0,-2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=7-2t \\\\ y=7 \\\\ z=7t\\end{aligned}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-128375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,0,-2⟩.$ From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨-2,0,7⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨-2,0,7⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,0,7⟩ & =⟨3,0,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,0,7⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,0,7⟩ & =-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,0,7⟩ & =-20 \\\\ -2x+7z & =-20 \\\\ -2x+7z+20 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-128375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b"} {"question" "q-128375" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-128375" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2x+7y-10=0"] ["math" "-2x+7z+20=0"] ["math" "-2y+7z+10=0"] ["math" "-7x+7y+7z-20=0"] ["math" "-x+7z+5=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-128375" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2x+7z+20=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-33923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the Cartesian equation $x-y+4z+16=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-33923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨1,-1,4⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+4z+16 & =0 \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{4}x+\\frac{1}{4}y-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=-4.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-4)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-4⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-4⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-1,4⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-33923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b"} {"question" "q-33923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-33923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(r-⟨0,0,-1⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,0,4⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,-4⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-1,4⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨-1,-1,16⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-1,4⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,4⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-1,4⟩=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-33923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(r-⟨0,0,-4⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-1,4⟩=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-128380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the Cartesian equation $4x+4y-2z=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-128380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨4,4,-2⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+4y-2z & =0 \\\\ 2z & =4x+4y \\\\ z & =2x+2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=0.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,0)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,-2⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-128380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b"} {"question" "q-128380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-128380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨-4,4,-2⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,-2,4⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,-2⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,4,-4⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,2⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,2⟩=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-128380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,-2⟩=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-70818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the Cartesian equation $2x+y-2z-4=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-70818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨2,1,-2⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z-4 & =0 \\\\ -2z & =-2x-y+4 \\\\ z & =x+\\frac{1}{2}y-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=-2.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-2)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,1,-2⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-70818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b"} {"question" "q-70818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-70818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,-2,-4⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,1,-2⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,2⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,0,-1⟩=0"] ["math" "(r-⟨0,0,2⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,1,-2⟩=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e04658479f49bbd05387a621e48423098a3ef7c96d9cc4b97acaa9d66dbcee7"} {"question" "q-70818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,1,-2⟩=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-ca